              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+future+cone"} closed future cone
              of the origin.
          %p
          #CausalPropagatorIsSkewSymmetric.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
                is skew-symmetric)
              %br/
              Under reversal of arguments the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+causal+propagators"} advanced and retarded causal propagators
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedRetardedPropagatorsForKleinGordonOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              are related by
            #eq:AdvancedAndRetardedPropagatorTurnIntoEachOtherUnderSwitchingArguments.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (19)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ±
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ∓
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_{\pm}(y-x) = \Delta_\mp(x-y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              It follows that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CausalPropagator"} (?)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \coloneqq \Delta_+ - \Delta_-
              is skew-symmetric in its arguments:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_S(x-y) = - \Delta_S(y-x)
                    \\,.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedRetardedPropagatorsForKleinGordonOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              we have with
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ModeExpansionForMinkowskiAdvancedRetardedPropagator"} (10)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo ±
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo −
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mfrac
                                        %mrow
                                          %mo ±
                                          %mi i
                                        %mrow
                                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                          %mn 2
                                          %mi π
                                          %msup
                                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                            %mi p
                                      %mo ∫
                                      %mfrac
                                        %mn 1
                                        %mrow
                                          %mn 2
                                          %mi ω
                                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                          %mover
                                            %mi k
