                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_F(x,y) = \Delta_F(y,x)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_18 Proof
            %p
              By equation
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AdvancedAndRetardedPropagatorTurnIntoEachOtherUnderSwitchingArguments"} (19)
              in cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CausalPropagatorIsSkewSymmetric"}
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+ + \Delta_-
              is symmetric, and equation
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RealAndSymmetricH"} (25)
              in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SkewSymmetricPartOfHadmrdPropagatorIsCausalPropagatorForKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is symmetric.
