            %p
              The second term is computed in a directly analogous fashion: The integrals
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_\pm
              from
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheTwoSpecialFunctionIntegralsInTheComputationOfTheCausalPropagatorIn3Plus1DOnMinkowski"} (28)
              are now
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo ±
                    %mo ≔
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
