            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SingularSupportOfCausalPropagatorForKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetimeIsTheLightCone"}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+support"} singular support
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_S
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone"} light cone
            %p
              Since the causal propagator is a solution to the homogeneous Klein-Gordon equation, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagation+of+singularities+theorem"} propagation of singularities theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropagationOfSingularitiesTheorem"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vectors"} wave vectors
              in the wave front set are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lightlike"} lightlike
            %p
              To that end, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi cp
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in C^\infty_{cp}(\mathbb{R}^{p,1})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+function"} bump function
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+support"} compact support
              includes the origin.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
              a point on the light cone, we need to determine the decay property of the Fourier transform of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto b(x-a)\Delta_S(x)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+of+distributions"} convolution of distributions
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi μ
                        %msup
                          %mi a
                          %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat b(k)e^{i k_\mu a^\mu}
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo ^
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat \Delta_S(k)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CausalPropagatorAsFourierTransformOfDeltaDistributionOnTransformedKGOperator"}
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ^
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∝
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi μ
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi μ
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi m
                                %mi c
                              %mi ℏ
                          %mo )
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mi sgn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat \Delta_{S}(k)
                    \\;\propto\;
                    \\delta\left( -k_\mu k^\mu - \left( \tfrac{m c}{\hbar} \right)^2 \right)
                    sgn(k_0)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that the convolution product is the smearing of the mass shell by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi b
                        %mo ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi μ
                          %msup
                            %mi a
                            %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat b(k)e^{i k_\mu a^\mu}
            %p
              Since the mass shell asymptotes to the light cone, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi μ
                        %msup
                          %mi a
                          %mi μ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{i k_\mu a^\mu} = 1
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              on the light cone (given that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is on the light cone), this implies the claim.
            %p
              Now for the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
            %p
              By def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardHadamardDistributionOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              its Fourier transform is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ^
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∝
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi μ
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi μ
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi m
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat \Delta_H(k)
                    \\;\propto\;
                    \\delta\left( k_\mu k^\mu + m^2 \right) \Theta( -k_0 )
            %p
              Moreover, its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+support"} singular support
              is also the light cone (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SingularSupportOfHadamardPropagatorForKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetimeIsTheLightCone"}
            %p
              Therefore now same argument as before says that the wave front set consists of wave vectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              on the light cone, but now due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/step+function"} step function
              factor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta(-k_0)
              it must satisfy
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq - k_0 = k^0
            %p
              Finally regarding the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            %p
              by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModeExpansionForFeynmanPropagatorOfKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              the Feynman propagator coincides with the positive frequency Wightman propagator for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^0 \gt 0
              and with the “negative frequency Hadamard operator” for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^0 \lt 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WF(\Delta_F)
              now follows directly with that of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WF(\Delta_H)
              above.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#DiracEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetimePropagators
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equation"} Dirac equation
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            We now discuss how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (example
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GreenHyperbolicDiracOperator"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            discussed above.
          #DiracEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetimeAdvancedAndRetardedPropagators.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_33 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+propagator"} advanced and retarded propagator
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equation"} Dirac equation
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+slash+notation"} Feynman slash notation
              reads
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi m
                                  %mi c
                                %mi ℏ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi i
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mfrac
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %msup
                                  %mi x
                                  %mi μ
                            %mo +
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi m
                                  %mi c
                                %mi ℏ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    D
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \-i {\partial\!\!\!/\,}
                    + \tfrac{m c}{\hbar}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \-i \gamma^\mu \frac{\partial}{\partial x^\mu} + \tfrac{m c}{\hbar}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+propagators"} advanced and retarded propagators
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedAndRetardedGreenFunctions"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives+of+distributions"} derivatives of distributions
              of the advanced and retarded propagators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_\pm
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedRetardedPropagatorsForKleinGordonOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo +
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\partial\!\!\!/\,} + m
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ±
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo −
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mi c
                          %mi ℏ
                      %mo )
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ±
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_{D, \pm}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left(
                    \-i{\partial\!\!\!/\,} - \tfrac{m c}{\hbar}
                    \\right)
                    \\Delta_{\pm}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the same is true for the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo −
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mi c
                          %mi ℏ
                      %mo )
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_{D, S}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left(
                    \-i{\partial\!\!\!/\,} - \tfrac{m c}{\hbar}
                    \\right)
                    \\Delta_{S}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_26 Proof
            %p
              Applying a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
              does not change the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+of+a+distribution"} support of a distribution
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedAndRetardedGreenFunctionsForGreenHyperbolicOperatorAreUnique"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+self-adjoint+differential+operator"} formally self-adjointness
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              (as for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TranslationInvariantKleinGordonPropagatorsOnMinkowskiSpacetime"} (11)
              implies that it is sufficent to check that applying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              to the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{D, \pm}
              yields the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi i
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo +
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi m
                                    %mi c
                                  %mi ℏ
                              %mo )
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mrow
                                %mi D
                                %mo ,
                                %mo ±
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mi i
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∂
                                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %mo +
                                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                      %mfrac
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi m
                                          %mi c
                                        %mi ℏ
                                    %mo )
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mi i
